      en: "The Lowveld Plain in Eswatini is a low-lying region east of the Middleveld, with an average elevation of 200 meters. Covering approximately 30% of the country, it is characterized by savanna vegetation and a subtropical climate. The area receives 500–700 mm of rainfall annually, concentrated in summer. Major rivers include the Great Usutu and Mbuluzi, which provide water for irrigation. Agriculture dominates, with sugarcane and citrus plantations covering large tracts. The region hosts Hlane Royal National Park, a protected area for elephants and lions. Soils are predominantly sandy loam, prone to erosion. Mining activities include coal and diamond extraction.",
